flowchart TD

  subgraph L0["Level 0 · Question"]
    Q["<b>Why did China's tariffs devastate some U.S. exports<br/>but have limited effects on others?</b><br/><i>Brad Setser, CFR, June 2019</i>"]
  end

  subgraph L1["Level 1 · Priors & assumptions"]
    P1["<b>Tariff effects are sector-specific</b><br/>Substitution and market structure determine the aggregate impact"]
    P2["<b>Bilateral trade ≠ total trade</b><br/>Lost sales to China may be redirected elsewhere"]
    P3["<b>Retaliation requires viable substitutes</b><br/>China cannot easily stop buying essential imports"]
  end

  subgraph L2["Level 2 · Evidence"]
    D1["<b>Commodity exports to China down >60%</b><br/>Much larger decline than manufacturing exports"]
    D2["<b>Soy exports effectively collapsed</b><br/>Farmers could not replace lost Chinese demand elsewhere"]
    D3["<b>Oil exports to China collapsed</b><br/>But total U.S. oil exports were largely unaffected"]
    D4["<b>Auto exports responded to the tariff</b><br/>Exports fell, then rebounded when China suspended it"]
    D5["<b>Manufacturing decline surprisingly modest</b><br/>Aggregate exports show little obvious tariff break"]
    D6["<b>China lacks substitutes in some sectors</b><br/>Aircraft and export-related inputs are poor retaliation targets"]
  end

  subgraph L3["Level 3 · Mechanisms"]
    M1["<b>Few alternative buyers magnify the shock</b><br/>Lost Chinese demand becomes lost total exports"]
    M2["<b>Alternative buyers divert trade</b><br/>Sales shift markets without reducing total exports"]
    M3["<b>Lack of substitutes weakens retaliation</b><br/>Chinese firms continue buying needed U.S. goods"]
    M4["<b>Other demand can absorb export losses</b><br/>Domestic sales or localization cushion production"]
  end

  subgraph L4["Level 4 · Intermediate claims"]
    C1["<b>Soy retaliation was unusually effective</b><br/>Bilateral losses became aggregate export losses"]
    C2["<b>Oil retaliation mostly redirected trade</b><br/>Bilateral trade fell without much aggregate effect"]
    C3["<b>Manufacturing retaliation was weaker</b><br/>China had limited leverage in several key sectors"]
    C4["<b>Identical tariffs need not have identical effects</b><br/>Sector structure changes the transmission"]
  end

  subgraph L5["Level 5 · Conclusion"]
    K["<b>Main claim: don't equate bilateral trade with aggregate impact</b><br/>The economic effect of tariffs depends heavily<br/>on substitution possibilities and sector structure"]
  end

  subgraph L6["Level 6 · Dialectic"]
    QF1["<b>Coverage caveat</b><br/>China had not tariffed all major U.S. manufacturing exports"]
    QF2["<b>Timing caveat</b><br/>China may have preserved targets for future retaliation"]
    R1["<b>Auto counterfactual</b><br/>SUV demand and production localization also affected output"]
  end

  P1 --> M1
  P1 --> M2
  P2 --> M2
  P3 --> M3

  D2 --> M1
  M1 --> C1

